  user_input {
    user_response: "User prompt: You are a senior full-stack engineer. Build a demo News Portal web app that is inspired by common Indian news portals (ABP Live style) but does not copy any copyrighted assets, logos, or exact UI. Use placeholders and original styling.\n\n0) Output format requirements\nOutput a complete file tree and then provide full code for each file.\nUse Next.js 15+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS.\nMake it runnable with:\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\nInclude a README.md with setup + deployment steps (Vercel).\nKeep code clean, modular, and production-like (but using demo data).\n1) UI/UX goals (ABP-style inspired)\nCreate a fast, responsive, card-based news UI with:\n\nSticky header with logo text (no real logo), Hindi/English bilingual labels\nPrimary nav: categories (desktop horizontal), mobile hamburger drawer\nBreaking News ticker (animated marquee) below header\nHomepage layout:\nHero lead story (big card)\nSecondary stories grid\nCategory sections (each with 3 story cards + \342\200\234More\342\200\235 link)\nTrending/Most Read sidebar on desktop (or a top widget on mobile)\nAd placeholders (clearly labeled \342\200\234Ad Slot (Demo)\342\200\235)\nArticle page layout:\nBreadcrumbs\nTitle, author, time, share buttons\nHero image\nContent body with paragraphs\nRelated stories\nCategory page:\nCategory title\nStory cards grid\nPagination or \342\200\234Load more\342\200\235 button (demo)\nSearch page:\nSearch input with instant results (client-side)\nOptional filters: category dropdown\nVideo page:\nVideo list with thumbnails\nVideo detail page with embedded YouTube iframe (demo IDs)\nPhoto gallery:\nGallery list page\nGallery detail page with simple slideshow/next-prev\n2) Design system\nColor palette inspired by news portals:\nPrimary: red (#e11d48 or similar)\nNeutral: white, gray-50..900\nBreaking bar: black background with red \342\200\234Breaking\342\200\235 badge\nTypography:\nUse system fonts + optional Google fonts\nMust look good for Hindi (Devanagari): include Noto Sans Devanagari or Hind (either via next/font/google)\nSpacing: consistent, readable, mobile-friendly tap targets\n3) Data layer (Demo / Mock)\nNo real backend required for demo.\n\nCreate a src/data/demo.ts with:\ncategories (6\342\200\22310)\narticles (20+) with:\nid, slug, title (Hindi), excerpt, category, author, publishedAt, coverImage (use picsum/unsplash), tags, body paragraphs, isBreaking, isTrending\nvideos (8+) with title, youtubeId, category\ngalleries (6+) with 8 images each\nCreate helper functions:\ngetArticleByIdSlug\ngetArticlesByCategory\nsearchArticles(query, category?)\n4) Performance & SEO (demo-level but correct)\nUse next/image everywhere\nAdd per-page metadata using generateMetadata:\ntitle, description, openGraph\nCreate robots.txt and sitemap.xml (static demo is fine)\nUse clean routes:\n/ home\n/category/[slug]\n/news/[idSlug] (e.g., 123-title-slug)\n/search\n/videos and /videos/[idSlug]\n/photos and /photos/[idSlug]\n5) Components to build\nHeader (sticky, nav, mobile menu)\nBreakingTicker (animated; clickable headlines)\nStoryCard\nSectionBlock (category block)\nTrendingWidget\nShareBar (share links for WhatsApp, Facebook, X, LinkedIn using URL encoding)\nFooter\nOptional: Skeleton loading components\n6) Optional mini Admin (demo-only)\nCreate a very simple /admin area (no auth needed for demo) with:\n\nAdmin home: list of articles with status badge\n\342\200\234Create Article\342\200\235 form (title, category, excerpt, body) that stores to local state only (no persistence)\nProvide UI in Hindi/English bilingual labels\nThis is just for pitch; keep it lightweight.\n7) Constraints & safety\nDo not use any ABP Live branding, logo, or copy their exact HTML/CSS.\nUse only placeholder content and images.\nThe output must be complete and runnable.\n8) Deliverables\nFull Next.js project code with Tailwind\nREADME with instructions\nClean and consistent UI\nNow produce:\n\nFile tree\nCode for each file (one by one, with headings showing file path)\nREADME.md at the end\n\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
    items {
      text: "User prompt: You are a senior full-stack engineer. Build a demo News Portal web app that is inspired by common Indian news portals (ABP Live style) but does not copy any copyrighted assets, logos, or exact UI. Use placeholders and original styling.\n\n0) Output format requirements\nOutput a complete file tree and then provide full code for each file.\nUse Next.js 15+ (App Router), TypeScript, Tailwind CSS.\nMake it runnable with:\nnpm install\nnpm run dev\nInclude a README.md with setup + deployment steps (Vercel).\nKeep code clean, modular, and production-like (but using demo data).\n1) UI/UX goals (ABP-style inspired)\nCreate a fast, responsive, card-based news UI with:\n\nSticky header with logo text (no real logo), Hindi/English bilingual labels\nPrimary nav: categories (desktop horizontal), mobile hamburger drawer\nBreaking News ticker (animated marquee) below header\nHomepage layout:\nHero lead story (big card)\nSecondary stories grid\nCategory sections (each with 3 story cards + \342\200\234More\342\200\235 link)\nTrending/Most Read sidebar on desktop (or a top widget on mobile)\nAd placeholders (clearly labeled \342\200\234Ad Slot (Demo)\342\200\235)\nArticle page layout:\nBreadcrumbs\nTitle, author, time, share buttons\nHero image\nContent body with paragraphs\nRelated stories\nCategory page:\nCategory title\nStory cards grid\nPagination or \342\200\234Load more\342\200\235 button (demo)\nSearch page:\nSearch input with instant results (client-side)\nOptional filters: category dropdown\nVideo page:\nVideo list with thumbnails\nVideo detail page with embedded YouTube iframe (demo IDs)\nPhoto gallery:\nGallery list page\nGallery detail page with simple slideshow/next-prev\n2) Design system\nColor palette inspired by news portals:\nPrimary: red (#e11d48 or similar)\nNeutral: white, gray-50..900\nBreaking bar: black background with red \342\200\234Breaking\342\200\235 badge\nTypography:\nUse system fonts + optional Google fonts\nMust look good for Hindi (Devanagari): include Noto Sans Devanagari or Hind (either via next/font/google)\nSpacing: consistent, readable, mobile-friendly tap targets\n3) Data layer (Demo / Mock)\nNo real backend required for demo.\n\nCreate a src/data/demo.ts with:\ncategories (6\342\200\22310)\narticles (20+) with:\nid, slug, title (Hindi), excerpt, category, author, publishedAt, coverImage (use picsum/unsplash), tags, body paragraphs, isBreaking, isTrending\nvideos (8+) with title, youtubeId, category\ngalleries (6+) with 8 images each\nCreate helper functions:\ngetArticleByIdSlug\ngetArticlesByCategory\nsearchArticles(query, category?)\n4) Performance & SEO (demo-level but correct)\nUse next/image everywhere\nAdd per-page metadata using generateMetadata:\ntitle, description, openGraph\nCreate robots.txt and sitemap.xml (static demo is fine)\nUse clean routes:\n/ home\n/category/[slug]\n/news/[idSlug] (e.g., 123-title-slug)\n/search\n/videos and /videos/[idSlug]\n/photos and /photos/[idSlug]\n5) Components to build\nHeader (sticky, nav, mobile menu)\nBreakingTicker (animated; clickable headlines)\nStoryCard\nSectionBlock (category block)\nTrendingWidget\nShareBar (share links for WhatsApp, Facebook, X, LinkedIn using URL encoding)\nFooter\nOptional: Skeleton loading components\n6) Optional mini Admin (demo-only)\nCreate a very simple /admin area (no auth needed for demo) with:\n\nAdmin home: list of articles with status badge\n\342\200\234Create Article\342\200\235 form (title, category, excerpt, body) that stores to local state only (no persistence)\nProvide UI in Hindi/English bilingual labels\nThis is just for pitch; keep it lightweight.\n7) Constraints & safety\nDo not use any ABP Live branding, logo, or copy their exact HTML/CSS.\nUse only placeholder content and images.\nThe output must be complete and runnable.\n8) Deliverables\nFull Next.js project code with Tailwind\nREADME with instructions\nClean and consistent UI\nNow produce:\n\nFile tree\nCode for each file (one by one, with headings showing file path)\nREADME.md at the end\n\n\n\nHere is the full initial file tree for the application:\n/.env.example\n/.gitignore\n/index.html\n/metadata.json\n/package.json\n/public/assets/aistudio/.gitignore\n/src/App.tsx\n/src/index.css\n/src/main.tsx\n/tsconfig.json\n/vite.config.ts\n\nThe following dependencies are installed:\n@google/genai: ^2.4.0\n@tailwindcss/vite: ^4.1.14\n@vitejs/plugin-react: ^5.0.4\ndotenv: ^17.2.3\nexpress: ^4.21.2\nlucide-react: ^0.546.0\nmotion: ^12.23.24\nreact: ^19.0.1\nreact-dom: ^19.0.1\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nThe following devDependencies are installed:\n@types/express: ^4.17.21\n@types/node: ^22.14.0\nautoprefixer: ^10.4.21\nesbuild: ^0.25.0\ntailwindcss: ^4.1.14\ntsx: ^4.21.0\ntypescript: ~5.8.2\nvite: ^6.2.3\n\nKey file contents:\n\n--- /.env.example ---\n```\n# GEMINI_API_KEY: Required for Gemini AI API calls.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime from user secrets.\n# Users configure this via the Secrets panel in the AI Studio UI.\nGEMINI_API_KEY=\"MY_GEMINI_API_KEY\"\n\n# APP_URL: The URL where this applet is hosted.\n# AI Studio automatically injects this at runtime with the Cloud Run service URL.\n# Used for self-referential links, OAuth callbacks, and API endpoints.\nAPP_URL=\"MY_APP_URL\"\n\n```\n\n--- /index.html ---\n```html\n<!doctype html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n  <head>\n    <meta charset=\"UTF-8\" />\n    <meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\" />\n    <title>My Google AI Studio App</title>\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"My Google AI Studio App\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\"An application built with Google AI Studio.\" />\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\n  </head>\n  <body>\n    <div id=\"root\"></div>\n    <script type=\"module\" src=\"/src/main.tsx\"></script>\n  </body>\n</html>\n\n\n```\n\n--- /metadata.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"name\": \"\",\n  \"description\": \"\",\n  \"requestFramePermissions\": [],\n  \"majorCapabilities\": [\"MAJOR_CAPABILITY_SERVER_SIDE_GEMINI_API\"]\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/App.tsx ---\n```typescript\n/**\n * @license\n * SPDX-License-Identifier: Apache-2.0\n */\n\nexport default function App() {\n  return <div></div>;\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /src/index.css ---\n```css\n@import \"tailwindcss\";\n\n```\n\n--- /src/main.tsx ---\n```typescript\nimport {StrictMode} from \'react\';\nimport {createRoot} from \'react-dom/client\';\nimport App from \'./App.tsx\';\nimport \'./index.css\';\n\ncreateRoot(document.getElementById(\'root\')!).render(\n  <StrictMode>\n    <App />\n  </StrictMode>,\n);\n\n```\n\n--- /tsconfig.json ---\n```json\n{\n  \"compilerOptions\": {\n    \"target\": \"ES2022\",\n    \"experimentalDecorators\": true,\n    \"useDefineForClassFields\": false,\n    \"module\": \"ESNext\",\n    \"lib\": [\n      \"ES2022\",\n      \"DOM\",\n      \"DOM.Iterable\"\n    ],\n    \"skipLibCheck\": true,\n    \"moduleResolution\": \"bundler\",\n    \"isolatedModules\": true,\n    \"moduleDetection\": \"force\",\n    \"allowJs\": true,\n    \"jsx\": \"react-jsx\",\n    \"paths\": {\n      \"@/*\": [\n        \"./*\"\n      ]\n    },\n    \"allowImportingTsExtensions\": true,\n    \"noEmit\": true\n  }\n}\n\n```\n\n--- /vite.config.ts ---\n```typescript\nimport tailwindcss from \'@tailwindcss/vite\';\nimport react from \'@vitejs/plugin-react\';\nimport path from \'path\';\nimport {defineConfig} from \'vite\';\n\nexport default defineConfig(() => {\n  return {\n    plugins: [react(), tailwindcss()],\n    resolve: {\n      alias: {\n        \'@\': path.resolve(__dirname, \'.\'),\n      },\n    },\n    server: {\n      // HMR is disabled in AI Studio via DISABLE_HMR env var.\n      // Do not modify\303\242\302\200\302\224file watching is disabled to prevent flickering during agent edits.\n      hmr: process.env.DISABLE_HMR !== \'true\',\n      // Disable file watching when DISABLE_HMR is true to save CPU during agent edits.\n      watch: process.env.DISABLE_HMR === \'true\' ? null : {},\n    },\n  };\n});\n\n```"
