    summary: "The error message \"Cannot set property [x] of which has only a getter\" (where [x] is a property name, such as `fetch`) indicates an attempt to assign a value to a property that has been defined as read-only. This commonly occurs in JavaScript and is typically a `TypeError` in strict mode[1][2][3][4].\n\nHere\'s a breakdown of why this error occurs and how to address it:\n\n**Causes of the Error:**\n*   **Getter-only Property:** The most common reason is trying to set a value for a property that only has a getter method defined, but no corresponding setter method[1][2][5][6]. A getter allows you to retrieve the value of a property, but without a setter, you cannot change it.\n*   **Strict Mode:** This error is a `TypeError` and is specifically thrown in JavaScript\'s strict mode. In non-strict mode, such an assignment would often be silently ignored, which can lead to hard-to-find bugs[1][2][3]. Classes in JavaScript are always in strict mode[2][3].\n*   **Built-in Read-Only Properties:** Some global variables or object properties in JavaScript are inherently read-only (e.g., certain mathematical constants or properties of the `window` object)[4]. Attempting to modify these will result in this error. The `fetch` property on the `window` object is a common example where this error might appear, as `window.fetch` is a global API that cannot be overwritten[7].\n*   **`Object.defineProperty()`:** When defining properties using `Object.defineProperty()`, if you only specify a `get` descriptor and not a `set` descriptor (or set `writable: false`), the property becomes read-only[1][8][3][9].\n*   **Private Accessor Properties (Classes):** In classes, if a private accessor property only has a getter defined, attempting to assign to it will also throw this error[2][3].\n\n**Solutions and Workarounds:**\n*   **Define a Setter:** If you intend for the property to be modifiable, you need to define a setter method alongside the getter for that property. The `set` syntax allows you to specify a function that will be executed when the property is assigned a new value[6].\n*   **Avoid Overwriting Read-Only Properties:** If the property you\'re trying to set is a built-in read-only property (like `window.fetch`), you should not attempt to reassign it. Instead, if you\'re trying to mock or modify its behavior for testing, you might need to use different techniques suitable for that environment (e.g., a testing framework\'s mocking utilities).\n*   **Check for Typos or Incorrect Property Access:** Ensure you are not accidentally trying to set a property that shares a name with a getter, leading to unintended recursion or assignment attempts to the getter itself[10][11]. Sometimes, renaming a getter or the internal property it accesses can resolve the conflict[10][6].\n*   **Use a Different Internal Property:** When using getters and setters within a class, it\'s common practice to use a different internal property (e.g., `_propertyName`) to store the actual data, while the getter and setter manage access to the public-facing `propertyName`[10][11]. This prevents infinite recursion and ensures you are assigning to a writable property.\n*   **Review `Object.defineProperty()` Usage:** If you\'re explicitly defining properties with `Object.defineProperty()`, ensure that if you want the property to be writable, you either provide a `set` function or set the `writable` descriptor to `true` (it defaults to `false` if not specified)[8][9].\n\nSources:\n[1] [realityripple.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGjeeGqcqfw-VEm90ZwsWIcWTYgcUeJ0yfAFHIDYaIWkmmnpo0RvtqhruoP_T-hukDhHo_qSmNNe0Ec9Qxojflh87hglkOfEzxpPieERE80IZIB-FFjMOjJCPHhNJm9Qxuakx1ecdAyEgV3Cr8NJkQ2NDVy-RE9IFQYHIarkzNkZXfROjK0Hk3g)\n[2] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQE_Bnm9zcQnN0cPiZzXdVdL8w4SRH5D7WR4OsRfjR4sybVkAcMYfAYG398b1FYVCSsM9T6UvAN0sViKAvT0VoG5O-U6KQMHL8WDPCO-_iDZVd-KwFQ9oBG963NkH2QXO1R3SkllGUJRRTjdE6Yax6xmNC0SNR3-QMrCPT4WSCM_1F7lqlSMTfS3vcj7Zqmo)\n[3] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFRROKsIQ36a8wvtTfMT4wXMy1K0SQVQRGBFi-IUKK2F8gJnLhLqSUs-tmbxe1eCbGc8p7kYpVicRYOgYM0S6DKirlxwgKRH3Zp_cWR8cwZuTXZvut3XozJe9lMcG393nZfisIYN7IQps_Y4yM4hgTdbJYoa1bHPbgB2BxK5um7xDVvmRxFfFEsmyCbrvQ9dn2Bt355gY2AKdsXAfBzOTQTsJHThC7mViLZHgw=)\n[4] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEY2ZMjedx6s9fgDpCwxKhpV-xm3QqL1-katZ1IOdt2jDMaaBKe3B28dgJswxiYI2VidVFreLVObqi3x4317YeYKHDZVy5NruPwz8uxsR3vTMWi0TNknpKHBIKHPhx0PMQNAe93g5vnh9VvzHwg8ZxIVfoBVMBYr9nH-ApZEhUVPWgOtsjE64W-rsIMsQ==)\n[5] [geeksforgeeks.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFY57gHbKbg8r9Se0xrZcs0XAQGPETCHc5_3Wy0BjFL-dg8zry7PYySmB-9uDYhRTRfGV9m-DLfzv6YvnsJaxFdd9kvdJCh5S5esfdIl6ZTSeb3iQY8ea2btuwVmKeILFlkCx_rp5Z0go6BDPYm8d3tjSZJ8ZlhXNA2myY6Rgjbf8njhCCfx1HvEuCWKdqOubtLwnvRGtgN)\n[6] [bobbyhadz.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQENZ8vKY9dA9xOkrsfx3_k1Sj-dO1AiyHTXLmNxy7LmiYu26-fE5MasgRrAeVe7KaxVZZjnOrnNnzoKtxr5w8rD7VuaMj588ra-sTiMRverLd0WfXYt-IskTXlw0B-xVzXe2n9VWglZKWkZwOT209CI5WEyMVzz0UpbaTqC7nacANrwfie6ExuHWg==)\n[7] [google.dev](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFvS3j_IrEJDDpajDXru0RJxoeihG8709kkK5jZgTf2UiqQqRqiyULHVnpvDUOQaGc-2Gyys_MyXXTzEf8KsmH17uRECOfnTUczDyY7SIgOjmr_P1FJCqPxQibENwoa27xhRnLNhodyQ9VwiH0iE5aHlvcccGyKOmQmVOslbXKEEP7varasm6TzHcJ7hlGdjJWulZEtkVHnB5PRGoJcihq8nbEcCYO_Jacva1uchF5a)\n[8] [codeblocq.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYixEhFFVbtjEXWnTi3UDpJV5u8R5Dft0japPd6P5iKCOQVBKdfH7SrrgPvJPqkz5cXvK9IlH3xT57ui6tD4W5HBc9aNHDBtndMItgEOBVQmei7pMiXUuejrWArmJ1sLu4heMJxKTBuZ-yN_i_nEgGN1xQt1XQlybeMBeuOwe0)\n[9] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEioC7_sEd0siMB5P_g0uqq2Rynx1vkImLM4D3I-o71w9-s1WciVp4b9-QGVhhHrL6UoLe2D2frFxi_jrXZYx