    }
    web_documents {
      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEvaUsZaDy787_LQyOgsOn_d5Cj3FmAG5r3z88o6YPp0SBjt3Il86sMHygXiBlvOVim8oXc0OFpAwnFLS7i9W7dYXc8hmZ47K7F8EWGSMphJbRTQTbfjvw8-HUb3UR0QMfkuMT9JVIJl6czuTjSZTmT8DlzpCxfP9T45qjMUqNT8dLCmIk-DQX-FoGHLB78l3H0F3xBZEHzxppdWBBnSuTe9F54nMJXvk9rtKhijG-5Hs0="
      title: "stackoverflow.com"
    }
    summary: "The error \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" occurs in JavaScript when code attempts to reassign the `window.fetch` property. This error arises because `window.fetch` is a native, read-only property in modern browser environments, meaning its value cannot be directly overwritten[1][2].\n\nKey points regarding this error:\n*   **Read-Only Property** The `fetch()` method on the `Window` interface is a built-in browser API used for making network requests[3][4]. It is implemented with only a \"getter,\" which allows its value to be read but not modified or reassigned[1][5]. This design prevents accidental or malicious alteration of core browser functionality.\n*   **Causes** This error typically occurs when a script tries to assign a new function or value directly to `window.fetch`, for example: `window.fetch = myCustomFetchFunction;`[6]. This might happen in scenarios such as:\n    *   **Polyfills or Shims:** An outdated or incorrectly implemented polyfill for `fetch` might attempt to redefine it without proper checks.\n    *   **Interception Libraries:** Libraries aiming to intercept or modify network requests for purposes like logging, caching, or authentication might try to override `fetch` directly.\n    *   **Testing Frameworks:** In some testing environments, there might be an attempt to mock `fetch` by direct assignment.\n*   **Strict Mode** This `TypeError` is specifically thrown in strict mode, which is common in modern JavaScript modules and classes. In non-strict mode, such an assignment might be silently ignored[1].\n\n**Potential Workarounds and Solutions:**\n\nInstead of directly reassigning `window.fetch`, which is not allowed, developers can use alternative patterns to achieve similar interception or modification goals:\n*   **Using a `Proxy` Object:** A robust way to intercept `fetch` calls without overwriting the original property is to use a `Proxy`. This allows you to wrap the native `fetch` function and inject custom logic before or after it executes, while still calling the original `fetch` functionality[7].\n*   **Service Workers:** For advanced control over network requests, such as caching, offline capabilities, or request modification, Service Workers are the recommended browser API. They operate in the background and can intercept all network requests, including those made with `fetch`, without directly touching `window.fetch`[6].\n*   **Saving a Reference:** If a third-party script is causing the issue by attempting to overwrite `fetch`, and you need to preserve the original, you might try to save a reference to `window.fetch` early in your application\'s lifecycle before other scripts have a chance to run: `const originalFetch = window.fetch;`[8].\n*   **Reviewing Third-Party Libraries:** If the error originates from a third-party library, check for updates, configuration options that disable `fetch` interception, or known compatibility issues[2][9].\n\nSources:\n[1] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFinot4AXquZmx__UExw4BXcvRFikZDHutLvVFAZbCxSOJJHt2x00Z2sdhZgPQA0kXaIWkmecUCNB2hfQXdI04uTWJkBwoMraTdG7m3DY6UZ1bnfwHDggjXUDyPtKLz1hsLERBRO9KTfmikXYWa8NIp5kpUDizEkMqMr-rgHrLPhOphsZS83DKnpivHxTji)\n[2] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEfQXDEbyH0giNDzDx_hjv0U2-hkOCR4MmHVOXpXu7EHN7ggH0pAsfIrG6Vx9T7yxm0S3cCY3v-Ng4-uM60mSKVjOF7cKyE5HYRnXOOAE9pW_IPh4W-bBoB7GdDXsTLOhGOG6si60PC-fPc)\n[3] [mozilla.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHeSiFPAF-T9pb7nQSACjDYwHvNf4krpl38-HxtDrzWRSzhK3ZI_cmy-mD4RWpOdIXCMLwVFhZERNAslN_nHgeGAMHw5jVC2l7YZWeakzb0a6w0YRAXI5oCtGwaJVaK0n9KEEWXpFcL08FqO025VP0-M7vh1hF2lQ==)\n[4] [freecodecamp.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFQyon7CNHlA5F8q2E21lEAursTYsdRlNvCHhljRWJgsY_GxXsoQDiYw8PmAFg3NDQEMCviinXdPJtWtXdF3JQabdyZRIPidYcS2RoavjtkxFfaR-bXboLSLHVXoRxFuPc5FKfQEydkCH4U5iUIUfaX97J5Lj04yPxF0PqRWPoQwbq98Gs=)\n[5] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFYU82xS94SOAJsLoDOHADA0JZN_UcfGVuvLq3j7-7nak7R-W5r4SDcNbi-6OQ33zKAE2R0dYfrb1aMR5jQDFzSqLPzE1v27PFITmH8v7grHees1Zjnq5H1c0swXXjwgbr58ddqHh9R7o3KJQs8oW1C1tiluIgGyr2Qf3Z1m_5MLY1YnmhvgTmyUsGFv0bXgdP6lgWNdpGk5JTUN50QVwU=)\n[6] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEO3RFRNa_vKeU40Dc0MvhSL8DpihjVA5J9pbuthgk_wxSCOjliBKDSpOVqCb7k55vKg10NcAgHCNBdEYaKTfcwWjVAqxyTPjOMDYzMZILYEw590DVz5sbgF2ObElkjhmwaDJ3Bf6WKTYPkqFzG53qXQI05T9KMlQ==)\n[7] [dev.to](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHD7urH_zbqs8Kv3OtlLojz74kRyJ18H6tYsqaCnhwsew6NttS-iLqH5M90sKK2XuNSPz6A2JFl-rCilebHWs6IW1hIjhQzB6aNhKEtlSqeEzmV1PEIur_1VrAOoPLer3A4PcsWZ3jobk_fOMVhQ5nApGYt0TobAwxGAeYALdTaylzqKko=)\n[8] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHvJWKf-20Kv04U69B68NyZyPXxGORbsy1b5YafXZnFKXP3HOfSL3PsL-tdm0mu8Ewu9m370p5PX9xpNkq1mrsPC7LBw5t-ccO5I1Lpo1O8Oqxw3GGcDNlDo-dm6viUgv2TI5xqargCo76bWRI566Bi75njhAzBd7D069MDZ5kHQcz6qkexqNZCJAqY4Mcp4kxGbsTGCqYhSZ0OclLQOuIJ7g==)\n[9] [stackoverflow.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEvaUsZaDy787_LQyOgsOn_d5Cj3FmAG5r3z88o6YPp0SBjt3Il86sMHygXiBlvOVim8oXc0OFpAwnFLS7i9W7dYXc8hmZ47K7F8EWGSMphJbRTQTbfjvw8-HUb3UR0QMfkuMT9JVIJl6czuTjSZTmT8DlzpCxfP9T45qjMUqNT8dLCmIk-DQX-FoGHLB78l3H0F3xBZEHzxppdWBBnSuTe9F54nMJXvk9rtKhijG-5Hs0=)"
