      url: "https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHd3JZX-GS2MuabTGafcIZj4jI-8sHdvxp0H_lS0pmSV_HM56nMIYLKr3TxFPMUv6iQpsAdXOzLkOn0_zKpODLaTgksqJxSSYKEJNWGHEtjzBrC9FSkf9nRM3OwaNt6K4Frro5yjuIqXuAf"
      title: "github.com"
    }
    summary: "The error \"Cannot set property fetch of\" typically indicates a JavaScript `TypeError` where an attempt is made to assign a value to a property of something that is `undefined`, `null`, or an object whose property is a getter (read-only)[1][2][3][4]. This error suggests that the object or variable you\'re trying to modify either doesn\'t exist yet, hasn\'t been properly initialized, or the property you\'re trying to set is not intended to be directly assigned[1][3][5].\n\nCommon scenarios where this error might appear in a GitHub context or related development environments include:\n\n*   **Uninitialized Objects:** Trying to set a property on an object that has been declared but not assigned a value (e.g., `let myObject; myObject.fetch = ...`) will result in this error because `myObject` is `undefined`[1][3][5].\n*   **DOM Manipulation Errors:** If JavaScript attempts to update an HTML element that hasn\'t loaded yet or doesn\'t exist, this error can occur. This can happen if `<script>` tags are placed incorrectly in the HTML, causing the script to run before the Document Object Model (DOM) is fully parsed[1][2].\n*   **Asynchronous Data Loading:** When data is fetched asynchronously (e.g., from a GitHub API), and the code tries to access or set properties on the data object before it has been successfully loaded and assigned, the object might be `undefined`[1].\n*   **Issues with `fetch` API:** Specifically, \"Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter\" suggests an attempt to overwrite the built-in `fetch` function on the global `Window` object, which is not allowed as `fetch` is a read-only property[4]. This can occur in environments like `vConsole` if conflicting libraries or scripts try to redefine global objects[4].\n*   **Framework-Specific Problems:** In development with frameworks like Next.js or Nuxt.js, similar errors such as \"Cannot set property query of #<IncomingMessage> which has only a getter\" or \"Cannot set property data of # which has only a getter\" have been reported. These often point to attempts to set properties on objects that are designed with getters, making those properties read-only, or when there are compatibility issues between framework versions (e.g., Express 5 with Next.js)[6][7].\n*   **GitHub Desktop Client Issues:** While often presenting as \"Cannot read properties of undefined,\" similar underlying causes can affect the GitHub Desktop application. Issues with corrupted installations or interference from antivirus software have been known to cause such errors, requiring a fresh reinstallation[8].\n\nTo debug and prevent this error, developers should ensure objects are properly initialized, use conditional checks before attempting to set properties, and consider modern JavaScript syntax like optional chaining (`?.`) or nullish coalescing (`??`) for safely accessing nested properties[1][3][5].\n\nSources:\n[1] [medium.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFH9imAXLTNa4FFX5YfnfLU7yeK1kkrcGX-vOWjhP5wqQydlnoqzKrU2l_YZZkEgzTT-qMXTcbvIKWhJ7T0jmwxHuuIDTrHkWXRzN9oqKgWs-5dC9kF1dgQSQ8OIyghToCemFFmjaFD1pjJWfBDGX3gdPra5g0aJdlgg2362qz2DWpXKyMhvb0o1HF3Ze6u6yiD36zRT26u8Rt2YhITxZvUg0onj2ve5l2Qv4LwrFxRMA==)\n[2] [kinsta.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEOUjHdRWIILd0SDmm_TwNlNDq-C-ARZ96ZE5OSg7PGUMlvst20i4Vmn09YOmRoM9M29WYXSdYPTLcgaeKMjsQ8wuVSN0N6z1XgnNaYH9lUDbawDqggzi1nOqkLpj_pLJpw-HwjmLXf6JKKy38TpUfwerHCB9dUcUbHPw==)\n[3] [geeksforgeeks.org](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHCwKZgUVlKYme8WPawjQDiDYwd6ApS0Q7AacrcVhGy2PZKxN6APFXKcSVxocGCbuIU0xlFAyWiKbDt1Ed2c_xU4TXqzPwA_8xoMFUjKSsvClghDKoBHM0u3W1s08FcJWKunGmpfzvGwSi89kIQl2jzHKnnR9HFBsSQCkbsma4IOnqLfluce_OMKGNJ09xCTWhPluZdxk9oU5M20RlF0djTo_QAOwZ5rw==)\n[4] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQEuJAxkWWlSEA9Yl44iBkzRLFFGd-uZt-daLXItW-Dt747UBX2GrH3W1Cl-Gnq-rNZ0nKZZ3GGI76YBbSrQSikrY0t_bSh-y4gwlva4RQRTAjfnqFsGgu8Brn5aB_AtwbLYUrLqWoc4LYA=)\n[5] [quora.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQGSU3WvWYDVt5cnVzuo0B7ZMEHP9UPp4BFIW2Cw99qtP3Noea0mOFNYvbTtOqOv8qbOWrVqd9CVm8v5VvWL8xmS9dWn6qSPKiZcYWe6roj96wFrqAV4TVpF4aJPFJaiJvRG6Cwgh2svNjYMOY9iylKzuE06X9mX47P9OPFBlDRdqnIvmYSIaGaObKPjqslOoio_cgc7fiF90KY=)\n[6] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQFHyXahGA46FDH2BBJYw1-EIGu7lqVrZA-5XoqDsoWZzmWZ-cNldCohL0N3CwD1NX89Luj0gZEAwEtKBCx30lS3zhokOZWuIZpD52-He14zdOKOCU8X0AF1vExNIW-7GYsDNuOUpkhuMIY=)\n[7] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHBDhG9Rt7V6gZ8WYT6IUD2S0BIkRJuzuPJtAhY7C-CrRFLJChr-8yOoEbYg_pRoInmeA_OUlWcerDFllZJohrKLw7AxfLb5W2DeS1jORaDbUKW_iiAXJ2h-aCkXKxRGFLhL5oo)\n[8] [github.com](https://vertexaisearch.cloud.google.com/grounding-api-redirect/AUZIYQHd3JZX-GS2MuabTGafcIZj4jI-8sHdvxp0H_lS0pmSV_HM56nMIYLKr3TxFPMUv6iQpsAdXOzLkOn0_zKpODLaTgksqJxSSYKEJNWGHEtjzBrC9FSkf9nRM3OwaNt6K4Frro5yjuIqXuAf)"
