    response: "I have identified and resolved the runtime `Uncaught TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter` error.\n\n### Root Cause\nIn modern browser environments and sandboxed preview iframes, `window.fetch` is configured as a getter-only accessor on `Window.prototype`. When preview harnesses, error tracking scripts, or network wrappers attempt to assign or rebind `window.fetch` in JavaScript strict mode, the engine throws an unhandled `TypeError` because no setter exists for the property.\n\n### Fix Implemented\n- **Global Accessor Definition**: Added an early execution shim in the entry point (`index.html`) and application root (`src/main.tsx`) that inspects the `fetch` property descriptor on `window` and `Window.prototype`.\n- **Bidirectional Getter/Setter**: Configured a delegating getter and setter that preserves the native browser `fetch` method while enabling any monitoring or interception tools to safely assign custom wrappers without crashing the preview."
    modified_response: "I have identified and resolved the runtime `Uncaught TypeError: Cannot set property fetch of #<Window> which has only a getter` error.\n\n### Root Cause\nIn modern browser environments and sandboxed preview iframes, `window.fetch` is configured as a getter-only accessor on `Window.prototype`. When preview harnesses, error tracking scripts, or network wrappers attempt to assign or rebind `window.fetch` in JavaScript strict mode, the engine throws an unhandled `TypeError` because no setter exists for the property.\n\n### Fix Implemented\n- **Global Accessor Definition**: Added an early execution shim in the entry point (`index.html`) and application root (`src/main.tsx`) that inspects the `fetch` property descriptor on `window` and `Window.prototype`.\n- **Bidirectional Getter/Setter**: Configured a delegating getter and setter that preserves the native browser `fetch` method while enabling any monitoring or interception tools to safely assign custom wrappers without crashing the preview."
