  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Implementing Persistence**\n\nI\'m working on initializing `dynamicArticles` with `localStorage` for persistence! This will ensure any articles created, edited, scheduled, or deleted stick around even when the user navigates between pages. I\'m also adding to `src/data/demo.ts`.\n\n\n**Defining Article Properties**\n\nI\'m now enriching the `Article` interface to include a `PostStatus` field, handling states like \'published\', \'draft\', and \'scheduled\'. I\'m also adding `updatedAt` for tracking changes. Considering the core data points: `id`, `slug`, `title`, `excerpt`, `author`, `publishedAt`, etc. are crucial for article management.\n\n\n**Expanding Article Metadata**\n\nI\'m expanding the article schema! I\'m adding `imageCaption`, `imageAltText`, `tags`, `body` (as an array of strings), `keyPoints`, and flags like `isBreaking` and `isTrending`. I\'m also including `views`. Then, I\'m including WordPress-specific fields such as `status`, `scheduledDate`, `focusKeyword`, and SEO metadata. I\'m also considering content format.\n\n\n**Analyzing Content Quality**\n\nI\'m now focusing on a live scoring engine for content quality that\'s compatible with SEO plugins like Yoast and Rank Math, which means a focus on factors that search engines appreciate. I\'m exploring an interactive checklist, and considering all the details, from the focus keyword in headings, meta descriptions, and image alt text, to content length and keyword density.\n\n\n**Evaluating Content Quality**\n\nI\'m now diving into content quality metrics! I\'m integrating readability analysis, including Flesch Reading Ease scores and reading level classifications, along with average sentence length and syllable count. I am also working on grammar, spelling, and tone suggestions. I\'m also now analyzing content length and keyword density. I will also be on the lookout for duplicate content and repetitive phrases, too. And I\'m starting to create the user interface and interactive AI assistant. It will provide conversational interactions and confirmations for potentially dangerous operations.\n\n\n**Integrating WordPress Functionality**\n\nI\'m now fully integrating with the WordPress Admin Editor, enabling users to interact via natural language or visual controls with real-time synchronization. I\'m focusing on clean, modular file separation. This includes `seoCalculator.ts`, `wordpressAssistant.ts`, and component files. I\'m focusing on the NLP engine, supporting multiple languages and generating markdown responses for tasks.\n\n\n**Designing the Interface**\n\nI\'m now focused on the UI, building the interactive WordPress Article Management Assistant as a drawer with chat bubbles, avatars, and markdown rendering. I\'m adding a language selector, prompt chips, and a progress bar. Action buttons like \"Apply,\" \"Insert,\" \"Create New Post,\" and \"Audit\" are being implemented. Also I\'m working on the Post Editor with title, slug, format selector, and rich block controls. A live SEO score badge is also included.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 861396731
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
