    thinking: "**Consolidating Admin Functionality**\n\nI\'m focusing on integrating all the specified system functionalities into a designated section within the admin panel. The goal is a centralized, accessible location for these components. The structure is being designed to streamline user access to the admin tools.\n\n\n**Prioritizing Module Integration**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on integrating the 20 identified modules within the admin panel. Specifically, I\'m concentrating on `AdminPage.tsx`, which contains the current navigation structure, to create the most intuitive architecture for the user. I\'ll need to refactor the current tab structure and ensure smooth access to each component.\n\n\n**Designing AI Article Suite**\n\nI\'m now fully immersed in developing the \"AI WordPress Studio\" within the admin panel. I\'m building out modules for both article creation and update functionality. This includes defining all the steps necessary for both modules, such as basic information input and detailed SEO optimization elements. This will be the main entry point to streamline article management. I\'m focusing on user-friendly module switching and intuitive navigation.\n\n\n**Developing Article Workflow**\n\nI\'m now outlining the specifics of new AI modules. I\'m prioritizing the article management dashboard, including its statistics and quick action menus. I\'m also working on the SEO optimization module with its live checker and technical SEO considerations. A critical component is the deletion module, ensuring a safety-first approach with backup and confirmation steps. I\'m focusing on user-friendly dashboards.\n\n\n**Constructing Content Tools**\n\nI\'m now building out key modules. I\'m focusing on article scheduling and publishing with options for immediate, scheduled, and recurring posts, along with a pre-publish checklist and publishing status controls. I\'m also addressing category and tag management, offering features like auto-tag suggestions and bulk tag operations, with best practice guidance included. Next, I\'m designing media and image management, and analytics features.\n\n\n**Analyzing Content Performance**\n\nI\'m now incorporating performance analytics, including average position, impressions, clicks, and CTR, alongside top keyword identification and a comparison of the top 5 performing articles. I\'m also adding engagement metrics and a content gap finder module. Furthermore, I\'m integrating modules for user roles and permissions, content templates, auto-save and revision control, multi-language support, and a comprehensive integration and settings module.\n\n\n**Integrating AI Tools**\n\nNow I\'m focusing on the integration of AI-powered tools within the admin panel, specifically modules for content enhancement. I\'m prioritizing interactive elements such as a content expander, headline optimizer with alternatives, readability improver, and grammar/spell checkers. I\'m also planning a help section with tutorials, quick commands, and FAQs to enhance user experience. I\'m now mapping out access within `AdminPage.tsx`, building out the \"AI Management Suite\" section.\n\n\n**Mapping Module Integration**\n\nI\'m now mapping out and thinking about switching between key modules. Specifically, I\'m focusing on their placement within the AI Management Suite. I\'m prioritizing dashboards, the article creation wizard with step-by-step guidance, and the content template selection. I also need to make sure the SEO tools, scheduling, and AI enhancer modules are accessible.\n\n\n"
