  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Adding Router Integration**\n\nI\'ve been examining `WpAiSuite.tsx` and identified line 83 as a key integration point. I plan to incorporate `useRouter` from the `RouterContext` and `ADMIN_TRANSLATIONS` from the `adminTranslations` utils. This will allow the suite to utilize the application router and translation services more effectively. I will be incorporating these imports, and instantiating `const { lang, setLang } = useRouter();` within the `WpAiSuite` component.\n\n\n**Analyzing UI Text Elements**\n\nI\'ve reviewed how the `lang` and `t` variables will be integrated into the UI elements within `WpAiSuite.tsx`. Specifically, I have identified and made a list of lines where translation keys are used for the Top bar, Left Sidebar Navigation, and the Dashboard section. This comprehensive list details exactly how the application leverages the translation keys for displaying the text.\n\n\n**Detailing Translation Usage**\n\nI\'m now cataloging all the UI text elements within `WpAiSuite.tsx` that utilize the translation keys (`t`). My focus is on the dashboard section and the article creation wizard. I\'ve pinpointed specific instances such as the \"Published (Live)\" text, various metrics like \"Drafts\" and \"Scheduled,\" and also the labels for the article creation wizard\'s title, subtitle, and steps. I\'m noting the keys used for both English and Hindi versions to ensure full coverage of translatable strings. This also includes the traffic and SEO health analytics sections, and all their labels.\n\n\n**Mapping Translation Keys**\n\nI am now thoroughly mapping the translation keys within the article creation wizard across its steps. I\'m focusing on the category, word count, tone, and audience labels. Furthermore, the \"Next Step\" labels are being carefully noted for accurate flow. Then, I am moving on to other sections such as the outline, WP metadata, HTML generation, and verification & publish. Finally, I\'ve mapped the template section, and now the on-page SEO section.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 599664281
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
