  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Analyze Initial Load**\n\nI\'ve been examining the initial page load when the admin opens the suite\'s page. I\'ve pinpointed that when `activeTab` is \'suite\', `<WpAiSuite ... />` is rendered. Further, I\'ve noted that `<WpAiSuite>` itself prominently features a dark banner displaying \"WORDPRESS AI ARTICLE SUITE\".\n\n\n**Review Module Integration**\n\nI\'ve shifted focus to module integration. I see \"12 Modules Integrated,\" with auto-save active. There\'s a Bharat Samachar banner and descriptive text. I\'ve noted a left sidebar with 12 module buttons with truncated text. The Dashboard module shows metric boxes, a terminal box, a device share bar, a search ranking box, and a quick actions bar. In `AdminPage.tsx`, I observe the top banner, metric cards, and navigation tabs above `WpAiSuite`.\n\n\n**Simplify the Presentation**\n\nI\'ve realized the core issue is the nested banners and redundant elements within the \"AI Management Suite\" tab, causing the cluttered interface. To address this, I\'m proposing a streamlined design. The aim is to eliminate the double banners and unwanted visual noise, creating a clean, user-friendly, and modern aesthetic, focusing on an intuitive UI/UX for the admin. I\'m thinking of a sleek, compact top header with essential actions.\n\n\n**Refine Interface Elements**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the interface elements, specifically the language switcher and metrics row. I think the badges are redundant so I am removing them. I also want to modernize the styling. I\'ve been reworking the tab navigation on `AdminPage.tsx` to streamline the user experience, emphasizing key functions. I\'m prioritizing clarity and a clean visual presentation. Now, I will look overhauling `WpAiSuite.tsx`.\n\n\n**Restructure the Sidebar**\n\nI\'m tackling the sidebar now, realizing the 12 cramped items are excessive. I\'m restructuring them into five focused sections: Overview/Analytics, Article Wizard/Templates, SEO/Content Enhancer, Media/Scheduling, and Taxonomy/Workflow. This clean grouping avoids truncation, reduces clutter, and improves navigation, giving the admin a better experience. Also, I\'m working to fix the labels in the dashboard.\n\n\n**Clarify Dashboard Labels**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the dashboard\'s labels to be clear and concise. The top four cards will now read \"Total Articles,\" \"Published Live,\" \"Drafts In-Progress,\" and \"Scheduled Releases.\" The secondary row will show \"Total Word Count,\" \"Avg. Reading Time,\" \"Top Category,\" and \"SEO Health Score.\" Finally, I\'m modernizing the traffic and performance section by replacing the black box with clean, visually appealing cards.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 5
      nanos: 26063454
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
