  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining the UI**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the `WpAiSuite.tsx` component. My goal is to revamp the UI for a cleaner, more modern look. I\'m starting with the top bar, aiming to replace the dark navy banner with a crisp white bar and a subtle slate border. This should avoid duplication with the admin page header and create a more polished aesthetic.\n\n\n**Updating the Top Bar**\n\nI\'ve made progress on the top bar in `WpAiSuite.tsx`. I\'ve added a white background, padding, and a subtle bottom border, along with some flexbox styling. I\'ve also incorporated a WordPress AI Suite label and a subtitle, along with some more styling, to match the updated look. I\'ve added a gray subtitle and a border. I am also working on the active article selector now.\n\n\n**Refining the Editor**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the article selector and editor buttons within `WpAiSuite.tsx`. I\'ve added a select dropdown for articles, truncating titles to fit the UI and providing a focus state style. I\'ve also incorporated styled buttons for opening the editor and assistant. Both buttons have been designed with improved visual hierarchy.\n\n\n**Reimagining the Layout**\n\nI\'m now overhauling the navigation. I\'m moving away from a cramped list to a cleaner, more modern approach. I\'m considering either a top sub-navigation bar or a streamlined sidebar with five easy-to-navigate sections. The five sections are dashboard, article wizard, SEO audit, media scheduler, and settings. Each section will have sub-tools represented as a clean toggle.\n\n\n**Defining the Menu**\n\nI\'m now focusing on defining a clear menu structure. The goal is an intuitive and modern experience. The idea is to present users with a streamlined sidebar, clearly displaying the core functionality. I am envisioning a structure with distinct sections for the Article Wizard, SEO Audit, Media Scheduler, and settings. Each section will provide quick access to sub-tools and features.\n\n\n"
